This means that the Tribunal should  consider and decide with reference to the evidence:
 (i) whether the disablement is permanent or temporary;
 (ii) if the disablement is permanent, whether it is permanent  total disablement or permanent partial disablement;
 (iii) if the disablement percentage is expressed with reference  to any specific limb, then the effect of such disablement of the  limb on the functioning of the entire body, that is, the Akhlesh (Dar) vs Imran Hussain (65/19Ac) on 16 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/16514734/
19  permanent disability suffered by the person.
